.TH LIBFAAR 3 "October 2026" "libfaar 3.0.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
libfaar, faar_create, faar_set_dither, faar_get_delay, faar_process, faar_flush, faar_destroy \- Polyphase Farrow-interpolated Kaiser-sinc audio resampler library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <faar.h>
.sp
.BI "faar_handle_t faar_create(uint32_t " in_rate ", uint32_t " out_rate ", uint16_t " channels ", faar_quality_t " quality ");"
.sp
.BI "int faar_set_dither(faar_handle_t " handle ", faar_dither_t " dither ", uint8_t " target_bits ");"
.sp
.BI "size_t faar_get_delay(faar_handle_t " handle ");"
.sp
.BI "size_t faar_process(faar_handle_t " handle ", const float *" in_samples ", size_t " in_count ", float *" out_samples ", size_t " max_out_count ");"
.sp
.BI "size_t faar_flush(faar_handle_t " handle ", float *" out_samples ", size_t " max_out_count ");"
.sp
.BI "void faar_destroy(faar_handle_t " handle ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B libfaar
is a lightweight, high-precision C library for digital audio sample rate conversion. It uses a polyphase filter bank with Kaiser windowing and Farrow cubic polynomial phase interpolation to deliver continuous, infinite-resolution fractional delays with >140 dB stopband attenuation and linear phase response.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.BR faar_create ()
Allocates and initializes a resampler instance for converting audio from \fIin_rate\fR to \fIout_rate\fR across \fIchannels\fR (1 to 8 channels supported). Quality presets include \fBFAAR_QUALITY_FAST\fR, \fBFAAR_QUALITY_GOOD\fR, and \fBFAAR_QUALITY_HIGH\fR.
.TP
.BR faar_set_dither ()
Configures dithering and noise-shaping error feedback (\fBFAAR_DITHER_OFF\fR, \fBFAAR_DITHER_TPDF\fR, or \fBFAAR_DITHER_SHAPED\fR) for quantization down to 16-bit or 24-bit integer PCM targets.
.TP
.BR faar_get_delay ()
Returns the resampler group delay in input frames per channel.
.TP
.BR faar_process ()
Resamples interleaved floating-point PCM audio samples.
.TP
.BR faar_flush ()
Flushes remaining pipeline history at end of stream.
.TP
.BR faar_destroy ()
Frees all allocated memory and resources associated with the resampler handle.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR faar (1),
.BR faac (1)
